# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and machine state. Regenerated by `hyphaed build`; some of it
# is tens of gigabytes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
out/
state/
*.deb
*.ko
*.o

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream and third-party source trees. These are CLONED, not authored here,
# and pinned by patches/VENDOR*.lock so a fresh checkout can fetch the exact
# revisions. Vendoring them into this repo would add ~200 GB and republish
# other projects' history under ours.
#   linux/, torvalds_linux/  , mainline kernel
#   github/                  , assorted upstream clones
#   kernel-patches/          , CachyOS/kernel-patches
#   linux-tkg/, linux-cachyos/
#   kernel-hardening-checker/, vex-kernel-checker/, kernel-research/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
linux/
torvalds_linux/
github/
kernel-patches/
linux-tkg/
linux-cachyos/
kernel-hardening-checker/
vex-kernel-checker/
kernel-research/

# Distribution tarballs and diffs fetched by the source phase.
*.orig.tar.gz
*.diff.gz
*.dsc
/update
patches/vendor/*.tar.*
patches/vendor/*.zip
!patches/vendor/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-specific probe dumps. These describe ONE box's hardware, and are
# regenerated by `hyphaed detect`. Useful locally, misleading in a repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
probe-output.txt
bios-settings-output.txt
gpu-link-output.txt
configs/base/boot-config-*
diagnostics/*.log

# Python
*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
copyfail-check/

# hyperresearch (per-project research vault). Local only: 38 MB of it is
# third-party PDFs fetched from arXiv, and the notes carry other people's full
# text. Our own prose about that reading lives in docs/research/ and IS tracked.
.hyperresearch/
research/
